<title>JAPAN: Moody's assigns Aa1 rating to Hokuriku Electric.</title>
<headline>Moody's assigns Aa1 rating to Hokuriku Electric.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said on Tuesday it had assigned its Aa1 rating to Hokuriku Electric Power Co Inc's $300 million worth of 7.0 percent notes due 2001.</p>
<p>Moody's said the rating was based on the firm's significance to the local economy, its important role as a power supplier within the Japanese utility industry, and its favourable industry operating environment.</p>
</text>
